Method	Code	Description	PMID	First Author	Year	Citation
CPM	cpm	Scaling to a million reads per sample.	15289482	Meyers	2004	Genome Research 14:1641
Total counts	total	Scaling to average number of reads in all samples.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
Median	median	Scaling to the median value.
Upper quartile	upperquartile	Scaling to top 25% expressed genes.	20167110	Bullard	2010	BMC Bioinformatics 11:94
Upper decile	upperdecile	Scaling to top 10% expressed genes.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
Housekeeping	guide	Scaling to a small set of pre-selected (housekeeping) control genes.	15543203	de Kok	2005	Lab Invest 85:154
geNorm	genorm	Scaling by minimizing the variance of 3-9 control genes, selected among housekeeping genes by a "gene stability" measure.	12184808	Vandesompele	2002	Genome Biol 3:RESEARCH0034
Stability	stability	Scaling by minimizing the variance of a hundred control genes, selected from the data by a "gene stability" measure.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
All Ubiquitous	allubiquitous	Scaling to the geometric mean of the expression levels of all ubiquitous genes.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
TMM	tmm	Trimmed Mean of M-values method.	20196867	Robinson	2010	Genome Biol 11:R25
Quantile normalization	quantile	Normalization of expression level distributions across samples.	19374774	Mar	2009	BMC Bioinformatics 10:110
Random	random	Mock normalization that scales each sample by a randomly picked factor.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
Total Ubiquitous	ubiquitous	Scaling to average number of reads in ubiquitous genes.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
Network Centrality Scaling	network,net	Scaling by minimizing the variance of a large set of control genes, weighted by network centrality.	24223126	Glusman	2013	PLoS ONE 8:e77885
